24
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:30,260
Alright everyone, let's begin.

25
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:33,060
Emily, let's imagine this situation.

26
00:01:33,390 --> 00:01:38,630
You just started a new job and your boss gives you a task you don't fully understand.

27
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:39,860
What should you do?

28
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:42,000
First of all, don't panic.

29
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:47,190
Many people think they must understand everything immediately, but that's not realistic.

30
00:01:47,170 --> 00:01:48,010
Absolutely.

31
00:01:48,350 --> 00:01:50,700
Even experienced employees ask questions.

32
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:57,010
One of the simplest and most professional phrases you can use is, Could you please explain this a little more?

33
00:01:57,050 --> 00:01:58,920
That's a fantastic phrase.

34
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:00,420
The meaning is simple.

35
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:03,850
You're politely asking your boss to give more information.

36
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,040
Let's hear a practical conversation.

37
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:12,130
Ryan, could you prepare the quarterly sales summary and organize the client feedback reports?

38
00:02:12,150 --> 00:02:12,410
Sure.

39
00:02:12,890 --> 00:02:16,230
Could you please explain the client feedback part a little more?

40
00:02:16,690 --> 00:02:18,760
I want to make sure I understand correctly.

41
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:19,560
Perfect.

42
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:21,800
That sounds professional and responsible.

43
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:22,680
Exactly.

44
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:26,550
Notice that Ryan didn't say, I don't understand anything.

45
00:02:26,970 --> 00:02:29,030
He asked calmly and politely.

46
00:02:29,490 --> 00:02:30,290
That's important.

47
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,080
Your tone matters.

48
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:36,650
Another very useful phrase is, I just want to clarify something.

49
00:02:37,170 --> 00:02:38,770
Excellent business English phrase.

50
00:02:39,250 --> 00:02:42,530
The meaning is, I want to make sure something is clear.

51
00:02:43,090 --> 00:02:44,160
Example conversation.

52
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:51,470
Of course, I just want to clarify something.

53
00:02:51,730 --> 00:02:56,090
Do you want the proposal sent only to the client or to the entire team as well?

54
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:59,110
That's a very professional way to ask questions.

55
00:02:59,670 --> 00:03:00,220
Exactly.

56
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:02,980
It shows you care about doing the work correctly.

57
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:07,310
Another common situation is when you're overwhelmed with work.

58
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:10,040
Oh yes, that happens to everyone sometimes.

59
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:14,020
Many employees feel afraid to tell their boss they're struggling.

60
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:16,720
But good communication is very important.

61
00:03:17,250 --> 00:03:22,030
One useful phrase is, I'm having a little trouble with… Nice and polite.

62
00:03:22,470 --> 00:03:25,350
The meaning is, something is difficult for me right now.

63
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:26,960
Example conversation.

64
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:30,380
Ryan, how's the database project going?

65
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:34,490
I'm making progress, but I'm having a little trouble with the reporting section.

66
00:03:34,910 --> 00:03:36,470
Could you guide me in the right direction?

67
00:03:37,010 --> 00:03:37,950
Excellent response.

68
00:03:38,450 --> 00:03:43,460
Notice how Ryan explained the problem clearly instead of simply saying, this is too hard.

69
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:44,200
Right.

70
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:47,770
Professional communication should be calm and specific.

71
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:52,010
Another useful phrase is, could you point me in the right direction?

72
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,860
I love this expression because it sounds natural and professional.

73
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:59,510
The meaning is, could you guide me or tell me how to start?

74
00:03:59,970 --> 00:04:01,130
Example conversation.

75
00:04:01,150 --> 00:04:05,490
Emily, I need you to prepare the client onboarding documents.

76
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:06,290
Sure.

77
00:04:06,350 --> 00:04:10,980
I haven't worked on onboarding documents before, so could you point me in the right direction?

78
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:17,470
Another important thing is learning how to ask for help without sounding negative.

79
00:04:18,630 --> 00:04:21,960
For example, don't say, I can't do this.

80
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:29,570
Instead, say, could you help me better understand this task?

81
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:30,590
Much better.

82
00:04:30,930 --> 00:04:32,050
Let's compare the two.

83
00:04:32,590 --> 00:04:34,910
Version one, this makes no sense.

84
00:04:35,130 --> 00:04:35,870
I can't do it.

85
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:38,520
That sounds frustrated and negative.

86
00:04:39,020 --> 00:04:42,550
Version two, could you help me better understand this process?

87
00:04:43,070 --> 00:04:44,970
Much calmer and more professional.

88
00:04:45,450 --> 00:04:46,030
Exactly.

